WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.847
agent-sim runs Apple's

00:00:01.671 --> 00:00:03.109
iOS simulator on

00:00:02.921 --> 00:00:04.052
a Linux VM

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.075
Armaan Jain open-sourced

00:00:05.887 --> 00:00:06.665
agent-sim

00:00:06.736 --> 00:00:07.844
which boots Apple's

00:00:07.668 --> 00:00:09.389
iOS simulator runtime

00:00:09.236 --> 00:00:11.630
on an x86-64

00:00:11.441 --> 00:00:12.832
Ubuntu VM via

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.941
x86Sim

00:00:14.107 --> 00:00:15.097
and gives agents

00:00:14.908 --> 00:00:16.123
a CLI and

00:00:15.993 --> 00:00:17.255
MCP server to

00:00:17.066 --> 00:00:18.056
install an .

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:18.528
ipa

00:00:19.054 --> 00:00:20.186
Setup takes about

00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:20.905
half an hour

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:21.636
and needs 8

00:00:21.448 --> 00:00:22.579
+ CPUs

00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:24.620
16 GB RAM and

00:00:24.431 --> 00:00:25.940
60 GB of disk

00:00:26.082 --> 00:00:27.037
it downloads the

00:00:26.943 --> 00:00:28.888
8 GB iOS runtime

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.478
from Apple

00:00:30.014 --> 00:00:30.874
It is early

00:00:30.722 --> 00:00:31.830
with no XCUITest

00:00:31.641 --> 00:00:32.466
support yet

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:33.976
and Apple's licensing

00:00:33.788 --> 00:00:34.601
for running its

00:00:34.413 --> 00:00:35.344
simulator off a

00:00:35.156 --> 00:00:35.992
Mac is an

00:00:35.816 --> 00:00:36.830
open question

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.364
Full story on

00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:39.071
the dashboard
